MP-03.1 — Webhook Verification

Technology learned:
HMAC-based webhook signature verification.

What I learned:
A webhook can include a cryptographic signature generated using a
shared secret and the webhook payload. The receiving server can
generate its own expected signature and compare it with the received
signature.

Test 1:
Used the generated signature as the received signature.
Result: True.

Test 2:
Replaced the received signature with "wrong-signature".
Result: False.

Key learning:
The server does not need to trust the webhook payload blindly.
It can verify that the sender knew the shared secret.
